$  | $+0.2$  | $-2.5$  | $-3.8$  | $-2.3$  | $+0.7$  | $+2.5$  | $-3.4$  | $-2.7$  | $-2.4$  | $+0.3$\nL591: Negative control, seed 2  | $-0.6$  | $-0.5$  | $-3.3$  | $+1.8$  | $-2.0$  | $+3.5$  | $+0.8$  | $-2.3$  | $-2.0$  | $-2.2$  | $-2.3$\nL592: Equal budget, ends  | $+1.4$  | $-0.7$  | $-1.0$  | $+2.4$  | $-1.8$  | $+4.0$  | $+0.9$  | $+1.9$  | $+1.2$  | $-1.4$  | $+0.6$\nL593: DeepSeek method  | HP std / mid  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\nL594: Uniform  | $-6.8$ / $+1.8$  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\nL595: Negative control  | $-7.0$ / $+1.1$  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\nL596: Interface-Full  | $+0.9$ / $+1.7$  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\nL597: Equal budget, ends  | $+1.6$ / $+3.4$  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\nL598: ## Appendix J Placement Batch\nL599: #### Design.\nL600: The batch answers two questions left open by the interface batch: how large the negative control’s gap is over several random placements, and whether some layout puts DeepSeek’s instruction away from the prompt ends while remaining sensitive to reduction. It ran on one H200 (141 GB) with vLLM 0.31, greedy decoding, full generation and one pass per frozen manifest, after a pilot on the same machine.\nL602: DeepSeek screen ($6\\to 3$). Four candidate layouts of 400 HotpotQA questions each, run with the unmodified model and uniform reduction only, put 10, 30, 100 or 300 words of unrelated text before the instruction.\nL618: 10 / 30 words before the instruction  | $-1.45$ [$-4.88$, $+2.01$] / $-1.87$ [$-5.10$, $+1.33$]  | descr.\nL619: 100 / 300 words before the instruction  | $+0.14$ [$-3.22$, $+3.49$] / $-0.18$ [$-3.42$, $+3.06$]  | —\nL620: DeepSeek-V2-Lite, standard layout, 400 questions\nL621: Interface-Full $-$ negative control (two placements)  | $+8.09$ [$+5.05$, $+11.26$]  | $<$0.001\nL622: Uniform $-$ unmodified  | $-6.79$ [$-10.16$, $-3.40$]  | descr.\nL623: First 1 / 8 full $-$ uniform  | $-0.42$ [$-1.71$, $+0.90$] / $+3.80$ [$+1.88$, $+5.88$]  | descr.\nL624: First 32 / 64 full $-$ uniform  