{\"rag_case\": case.to_dict(), \"corpus\": snapshot.to_dict()})\nL910: \nL911: ak.evaluate([s], model=\"precomputed\",\nL926: # {'tool_names_only': 1, 'none': 1} <- the report kept tool names, not arguments\nL927: \nL928: episodes = ak.episodes_from_agenttune(\"report.json\")\nL929: \nL930: result = AgentEvalRunner().run(AgentEvalSpec(\nL931: \nL932: mode=\"recorded\", episodes=episodes,\nL933: \nL934: scorers=[\"tool_call_f1_name\", \"tool_call_validity\"]))\nL935: \nL936: print(result.summary())\nL937: \nL938: # Verified success: 1/2 (1/2 decided) Failure: 1 Unknown outcome: 0 ...\nL939: \nL940: result.rows[0].ineligible\nL941: # {'tool_call_f1_name': 'case.reference_turns', 'tool_call_validity': 'case.allowed_tools'}\nL942: \nL943: write_sidecar(result, \"auditkit_sidecar.jsonl\") # one record per trajectory id\nL944: ### A.4  Command-line interface\nL945: \nL946: Listing 20: CLI: zero-configuration smoke test.\nL947: \nL948: ⬇\nL949: \nL950: pip install auditkit\nL951: \nL952: auditkit eval --model echo <<< \"What is 2+2?\" # zero-cost test double, no API key needed\nL953: \nL954: Listing 21: CLI: evaluating a built-in benchmark.\nL955: \nL956: ⬇\nL957: \nL958: auditkit eval --dataset mmlu --model openai:gpt-4 o --output results.json\nL959: \nL960: auditkit eval --dataset gsm8k --model openai:gpt-4 o --output results.json\nL961: \nL962: Listing 22: CLI: evaluating against a CSV dataset: any tabular data, any column names.\nL963: \nL964: ⬇\n"
